{
  "FormatVersion": 3,
  "Id": "e3cfa5d7-fff0-5f26-b8b3-32539f72c32b"/*RigidForceExample*/,
  "Description": "[RigidForce] pushes the dynamic bodies of a world. Three continuous forces make a whirlwind: a Vortex swirls the boxes around the vertical axis, a Radial force keeps them near the centre and a Directional force lifts them against gravity. A fourth force is an impulse: it fires once each time its Trigger is pressed.\n\nAKA: wind, vortex, tornado, attractor, gravity well, explosion, impulse, force field\n\nTips\n- Playback must run for the simulation to advance; press Reset on the World to start over.\n- Negative Strength turns a radial pull into a push.\n- ScaleByMass makes heavy bodies react less; Field samples a [VectorField], e.g. from [VolumeToField].",
